// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0, GPIO2 and GPIO15 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard
// pushbuttons SW3, SW2, SW1. Independently re-verified (2026-07-14)
// directly against the real RoboticsBrno/ArduinoLearningKitStarter-library
// GitHub repo (not just this repo's own copied pins_arduino.h):
// src/ALKS.h declares the ESP32-variant pin map SW1=15, SW2=2, SW3=0
// (matching this board's pins_arduino.h exactly); src/ALKS.cpp's
// setupButtons() calls pinMode(SW1/SW2/SW3, INPUT_PULLUP); and the
// official examples/boardTest/boardTest.ino and examples/buttonSetLed/
// buttonSetLed.ino sketches both digitalRead() these pins as buttons.
// (Corrects an earlier pass's citation of a nonexistent "test_fw.ino" -
// no such file exists in the repo; the real example sketches are
// boardTest.ino, buttonSetLed.ino, ledFade.ino and testAllLeds.ino.)
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO22, GPIO23 and GPIO5 tagged "led_high" - confirmed onboard
// discrete LEDs L_R, L_Y (= LED_BUILTIN), L_B. Independently re-verified
// against the real examples/testAllLeds/testAllLeds.ino, which does
// digitalWrite(L_R/L_Y/L_B/L_G, HIGH) to turn each on and LOW to turn
// each off (active-high) - and examples/boardTest/boardTest.ino, which
// toggles the same pins HIGH/LOW in its test loop.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO4 and GPIO21 tagged "led_r_high"/"led_g_high" - confirmed
// discrete 3-GPIO RGB LED channels L_RGB_R, L_RGB_G. Independently
// re-verified against examples/testAllLeds/testAllLeds.ino (digitalWrite
// HIGH turns each RGB channel on) and examples/boardTest/boardTest.ino
// (drives L_RGB_R/G/B HIGH when the corresponding button is pressed) -
// both confirm active-high. The blue channel L_RGB_B is on GPIO16, which
// is excluded from chipGpios on this chip (PSRAM-reserved) and so is
// left untagged.
